an have all your  government services online and the  ukrainian government really interacting  with western tech giants there to bring  in investment to bring awareness for  ukraine and what it has to offer so i  think ukraine is going to be  pushing trying to make it a bigger part  of its national economy it's  a sector that you know wars can't  readily destroy or you know uh put an  end to you know in its ability to to  create jobs and create investment so i  think that's something that ukraine is  really going to be pushing in the hope  to make basically the you know at the  new war status quo kind of more  palatable to ordinary ukrainians who  kind of have to find a way of going  about their daily lives living their  family lives  you know developing career at the same  time as  basically preparing potentially to go  off and fight you know if the government  calls on them uh you know uh months and  weeks down the line  i mean we use the phrase new normal  during the coven pandemic a lot arguably  overused it but i think it applies again  this time around to ukrainians and the  war that they are experiencing  laura turning to you what is your answer  to this question another six months of  war where is russia's economy going to  be  going to be in in a more tight position  that it's now  but certainly um  certainly still  still fairly wealthy  it's the bit longer term view  that is is especially gloomy for russia  um i fully fully agree that sort of the  ukrainian government is currently doing  a lot in in  in trying to plan the rebuilding of the  country and and  and trying to take full benefit of  integration with the western  western countries and  restructuring  much of  the economy  to to become more based on whereas  russia is doing exactly the opposite  it's it's isolating itself from uh from  most of the world it's isolating itself  from the global  scientific community  and it's it's uh  sort of really trying to build a  domestic economy  that's only reliant on domestic  domestic innovation that a  few of the future in the longer term  looks much bleaker leaker for russia and  for ukraine in this sense  well nick at least ukrainians will be  able to take some hope from that  that's all for our business special  looking at ukraine and russia's  respective economies as the conflict  slips into its seventh month many thanks  to my guests nick connolly and lara  solanco if you've enjoyed this video  remember to hit like and subscribe and  why not check out some of our other  stuff on our dw news channel on youtube  from me and the team goodbye and we hope  to see you again soon
 

